    "cross_check": {
      "cattle_beef": "computed national stock sum 9,541,765 head (2025) vs. an independently reported ~9.9-10.0M head figure for early-2568 (pasusart.com, \"'โคเนื้อ' ในไทย 4 เดือนแรก เพิ่มขึ้นต่อเนื่องแตะ 10 ล้านตัว\") — within ~4-5%, both are live-standing-stock counts (not throughput). PASS, high confidence.",
      "pig": "computed national stock sum 12,208,545 head (2025). A separately reported figure of 23.584 million for 2568 ('ปริมาณการผลิตสุกร') is an ANNUAL PRODUCTION/THROUGHPUT volume (pigs marketed across the whole year, ~2x turns on a ~6-month cycle), not a standing-stock count — not directly comparable, so no discrepancy is claimed either way. No independent stock-count figure was found to cross-check against; flagged UNVERIFIED-BY-EXTERNAL-TOTAL but geographically plausible (top provinces Ratchaburi/Kanchanaburi/Lopburi match Thailand's well-documented central-region pig belt).",
      "chicken_all": "computed national stock sum 516,975,571 head (2025). No independent aggregate stock figure was found to cross-check against (Thailand's commonly-cited chicken figures are annual broiler-slaughter throughput, ~1.5-1.8bn/yr, not a standing-stock count, so not comparable). Flagged UNVERIFIED-BY-EXTERNAL-TOTAL but geographically plausible (top provinces Lopburi/Chonburi/Kanchanaburi/Prachinburi/Saraburi match Thailand's well-documented broiler-industry belt)."
    },
    "warnings": [],
    "gaps": {
      "layer_broiler_split": "ABSENT. DLD's national CKAN dataset dld_01_0601 ('จำนวนไก่') reports ALL chicken types combined (broiler + layer + native + other) at province level — confirmed by enumerating every one of DLD's 36 CKAN datasets, none splits by chicken type at province granularity. A true ไก่ไข่ (layer) vs ไก่เนื้อ (broiler) province split exists only in DLD's 9 separate ปศุสัตว์เขต regional-office publications (e.g. region6.dld.go.th, region3.dld.go.th), each on its own subsite with unstable URLs — a sampled link (region6.dld.go.th/webnew/pdf/ict63/T6-1-Chick.pdf) 404'd within the same session that found it via search — and no guaranteed consistent per-year table format across all 9 offices. Stitching that into one national table is real, separate scope, NOT attempted here. 'layer' and 'broiler' are intentionally MISSING from species{} (not guessed from the combined total); the combined figure is kept under species.chicken_all so the real data isn't discarded."
    },
    "note_for_downstream": "species{} keys present: pig, cattle_beef, chicken_all. 'layer' and 'broiler' are NOT present — see meta.gaps.layer_broiler_split. Do not backfill them from chicken_all without a real per-species source."
